invariant: INV-16
file: ct.h
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: ct.h gives every file of a host object the native multiply, so the
  files under their own names, which a session without
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY runs, are the native copies again under
  other names. Every test that checks bytes passes, and the dispatch
  counts still split by name. test/widemul-builds.sh requires each file
  under its own names to compile to the same assembly with the host
  object's define as without it.

--- old
#if (defined(CH_NATIVE_WIDEMUL) || defined(CH_WIDEMUL_NATIVE_COPY)) && !defined(CH_CT_WIDEMUL)
--- new
#if (defined(CH_NATIVE_WIDEMUL) || defined(CH_WIDEMUL_NATIVE_COPY) || defined(CH_CPU_RUNTIME)) && !defined(CH_CT_WIDEMUL)
